{
  "an5.194:0.1": "Numbered Discourses 5.194 ",
  "an5.194:0.2": "20. Brahmins ",
  "an5.194:0.3": "With Kāraṇapālī ",
  "an5.194:1.1": "At one time the Buddha was staying near Vesālī, at the Great Wood, in the hall with the peaked roof. ",
  "an5.194:1.2": "Now at that time the brahmin Kāraṇapālī was working for the Licchavis. ",
  "an5.194:1.3": "He saw the brahmin Piṅgiyānī coming off in the distance ",
  "an5.194:1.4": "and said to him, ",
  "an5.194:2.1": "“So, Piṅgiyānī, where are you coming from in the middle of the day?” ",
  "an5.194:2.2": "“I’m coming, worthy sir, from the presence of the ascetic Gotama.” ",
  "an5.194:2.3": "“What do you think of the ascetic Gotama’s lucidity of wisdom? Do you think he’s astute?” ",
  "an5.194:2.4": "Worthy sir, who am I to judge the ascetic Gotama’s lucidity of wisdom? ",
  "an5.194:2.5": "You’d really have to be on the same level to judge his lucidity of wisdom.” ",
  "an5.194:2.6": "Worthy Piṅgiyānī praises the ascetic Gotama with high praise indeed.” ",
  "an5.194:2.7": "“Who am I to praise the ascetic Gotama? ",
  "an5.194:2.8": "He is praised by the praised as the first among gods and humans.” ",
  "an5.194:2.9": "“But for what reason are you so devoted to the ascetic Gotama?” ",
  "an5.194:3.1": "“Suppose a person was completely satisfied by the best tasting food. They wouldn’t be attracted to anything that tasted inferior. ",
  "an5.194:3.2": "In the same way, when you hear the worthy Gotama’s t